Feature: Hook Directives
  As a developer using godogen
  I want to generate hook registration code from godogen directives
  So that I can set up and tear down test state

  Scenario: Generate before hook
    Given a Go file "hooks.go" with content:
      """
      package example

      import "context"

      //godogen:before
      func (s *Suite) beforeScenario(ctx context.Context) (context.Context, error) {
          return ctx, nil
      }
      """
    When I run godogen
    Then the command should succeed
    And the file "hooks_initialize.go" should have content:
      """go
      // Code generated by godogen; DO NOT EDIT.

      package example

      import "github.com/cucumber/godog"

      // InitializeHooks registers steps defined in "hooks.go" with the [godog.ScenarioContext].
      func InitializeHooks(sc *godog.ScenarioContext, r1 *Suite) {
      	// DO NOT EDIT, instead edit the "//godogen:step <PATTERN>" directive
      	// of the respective function declaration.
      	//
      	// Note: there must be no space between the "//" and the "godogen:step",
      	// see "directive comment" in https://tip.golang.org/doc/comment#syntax
      	sc.Before(r1.beforeScenario)
      }
      """

